# Production (agents)

**Do not hunt for the host.** Same shared nginx box as Discendis / SRB Connect / Rollt.

**HARD GATE:** Do not rsync, git-pull, compose-up, migrate, or edit remote nginx/`.env`
unless the user explicitly asked to deploy or change production in this conversation.
Read-only SSH/psql/curl **is** allowed when they ask to look at prod.

Never use `sudo bash -lc 'cd ~/…'` (`~` becomes `/root`). Never `--remove-orphans`.
Never touch sibling stacks (discendis, srb-connect, rollt, staking.agency).

## Connect (Cloudflare is HTTP-only — do not SSH to temperatura.live)

```bash
ssh -i ~/.ssh/keys/priv/web -p 3008 -o IdentitiesOnly=yes elrond@45.128.116.8
```

- User **`elrond`**, key **`~/.ssh/keys/priv/web`**, port **3008**, origin **`45.128.116.8`** (`$THC3`)
- App: **`/home/elrond/temperature-monitor`** (git clone of this repo)
- Data: **`/home/elrond/temperature-monitor-data/pg`**
- Compose project **`temperature-monitor`**, file `deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml`, env **remote** `.env` (never rsync it)
- Nginx: `/etc/nginx/sites-available/temperature-monitor.conf` ← `deploy/nginx-temperature-monitor.conf`
- Containers: `temperature-monitor-postgres-1`, `temperature-monitor-api-1`, `temperature-monitor-web-1`

| Service | Localhost port |
| --- | --- |
| Web | **3030** |
| API | **4030** |
| Postgres | **5436** |

Public: `https://temperatura.live` · `https://api.temperatura.live`

## Inspect (read-only)

```bash
KEY=~/.ssh/keys/priv/web
SSH="ssh -i $KEY -p 3008 -o IdentitiesOnly=yes elrond@45.128.116.8"
$SSH 'cd /home/elrond/temperature-monitor && git log -1 --oneline && docker compose --env-file .env -f deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml ps'
$SSH 'docker exec temperature-monitor-postgres-1 psql -U tempmon -d tempmon -c "SELECT id, name, \"lastSeen\", \"lastSeenVia\" FROM \"Device\";"'
```

Local Docker on this workstation is **not** production (`tempmon-pg` on `:5434`).

## Deploy (only when asked)

Push `main` first. On the server, `git pull` then rebuild **only** the service that changed
(`web` / `api`; postgres almost never). `--env-file .env` is required (compose file lives in `deploy/`).

```bash
KEY=~/.ssh/keys/priv/web
ssh -i "$KEY" -p 3008 -o IdentitiesOnly=yes elrond@45.128.116.8 \
  'set -e; cd /home/elrond/temperature-monitor; git pull --ff-only;
   docker compose --env-file .env -f deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml up -d --build web'
```

API/schema: rebuild `api`, then `docker compose --env-file .env -f deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml exec -T api npx prisma migrate deploy`.
After nginx file changes: copy vhost, `sudo nginx -t`, reload; curl siblings to confirm they still answer.

Operator login is in the **remote** `.env` (`OWNER_EMAIL` / `OWNER_PASSWORD`), not the laptop `.env`.
